## THE MODE — read this twice

**CODE_PATCH.** This service runs **VITEST** (`vi`, not `jest`). Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files:
1. `services/api-gateway/src/routes/admin.ts` — ONE hunk that only INSERTS lines (no `-` line at all).
2. `services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1230-settings-write-validates-allowed-document-types.test.ts` — ONE NEW file.
**Nothing else.** Not `routes/verification.ts`, not `services/health.ts`, not `index.ts`, not any existing test. Two files, no more, no fewer.
Write the paths as `services/api-gateway/...` — NEVER `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/...`.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

`PUT /api/admin/settings` (`admin.ts:1123-1129`) reads the stored `platform-settings`, shallow-merges the request body over it (`:1126` `{ ...existing, ...body }`), writes it (`:1127`) and answers 200. It validates nothing. Each connector's document-type allow-list lives in that body at `integrations[].config.allowedDocumentTypes`, and the readers (`routes/verification.ts:1216-1230`, `services/health.ts:49-58`) look it up by exactly that path. Since KS-1204 the create path refuses EVERY create (403) for a connector whose stored allow-list is not an array, so an admin who saves a string, an object or an empty string locks that connector out of all creates and learns it only from the 403s. **This task (the ticket's own Recommendation): validate every `integrations[].config.allowedDocumentTypes` present in the body as an array of strings, BEFORE the merge and the write, and refuse a malformed body with 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` naming the path.** Absent stays allowed. **Decision this brief takes:** `null` counts as absent too, because both readers treat `null` exactly like a missing key (no restriction) and refusing it could break a client that clears the list with `null`.

NOT in this task: the `integrations` container itself when it is not an array (KS-1231, filed separately — the hunk only looks inside an ARRAY `integrations`); which admin roles may write (a comment on the ticket raises it as an intent question for the owner); the HTML-escaping on `/api/v1/admin/settings`; `workflowPolicy` or any other config field; anything touching auth, MFA or OAuth.

